# Chroma library, modern Earth: the arts sphere's events as they touch a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22" update
# stage 4, item 15 phase 3). Design: chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-data/arts.json (events with on_character and the modern epoch; each scene is built on the event's
# wording.modern and on_character). Face words: chroma-library/earth_spheres.py. Fields: build.py (the spheres' fields of
# world-fields.md, 2026-10-09).
#
# Every moment here is an event moment: a life event the Engine fires on its sphere event (sphere_event: <key>) for the
# people its selector names (place, members or all); per_year is all 0 and there are no drivers. The '# world:' line
# above each moment gives the event key, the selector and the share of selected people who meet the moment (estimate).
# Nineteen moments, one per arts event (all nineteen have on_character and a modern wording; none is answered by
# earth.py or the ready files). Tone follows the event's tone (good = joy, bad = trouble, mixed = mixed): 7 joy,
# 6 trouble, 6 mixed.
#
# Options: sphere: on each is the face the act is in (one-colour X: arts.X; a pair: its pair face in wheel order, so
# WR is arts.RW, WG arts.GW, UG arts.GU). Levers (lever:) where the act plainly is one, from character.levers.
# 'every song in your pocket' is the art and the makers' living under a new medium; 'everyone is suddenly on the new
# medium' (earth-world-eras.lib) is how people talk and are seen, and stays separate.
#
# Layout: each a life event with the five one-colour options and one pair set. The 19 use all twelve halves of D1 to D6,
# seven of them twice (D1a, D1b, D2a, D3a, D3b, D6a, D6b), each chosen to hold the event's own pair faces where it has
# them. Evenness: in every moment each colour's one-colour chance plus half its two pairs' chances is the same sum, so
# every colour has the same mean chance in each moment and in every stage. No flags.
#
# share: on every moment (2026-10-10, Engine phase 3a) is its '# world:' share: the engine draws at birth who can
# ever meet it, so when the event comes to town only that share of the people there are open to the moment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- new_sound (pairs D3b)

# world: sphere event new_sound, selector place, share .3
== a sound with no name yet
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: new_sound
share: .3
haunt: arts.song
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 8-25
times: World event: new_sound (sphere arts). Selector place: a new sound takes hold in a quarter with many young people, cheap rooms, newcomers mixing and a few venues willing to take a chance; about 3 in 10 of the people living near it are drawn in, or kept awake by it (share .3, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: youth, a cheap quarter with empty warehouses, newcomers mixing, a person who goes out to hear music
rarer: a settled quiet town, older age, long working hours
tone: joy
life: friends, interests, community
horizon: months
roles: friend
earth: a few clubs in the old warehouse quarter play a sound nobody has a name for yet, and the queue goes round the block
scene: A few clubs in the old warehouse quarter play a sound nobody has a name for yet. The queue goes round the block every Friday, and {friend} says it is the only place worth being.
scene W: Hundreds of strangers sing the same lines back at the band, as one voice. To {N} it sounds almost like a hymn.
scene U: Nobody can say how the sound is made: the beat is wrong and somehow right. {N} wants to know how it works.
scene B: The queue goes round the block and the clubs are tiny. Whoever opens a bigger room first will do well.
scene R: The bass comes up through the floor and {N} feels it in the chest. This is the sound {N} has been waiting for.
scene G: To {N} it sounds like noise, and the old songs had words a whole wedding could sing. Still, the young ones on the street talk of nothing else.
- W | help the club run a safe door, so every newcomer gets in and gets home | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: arts.W | chance: 69
- U | learn how the sound is made, and try it on a borrowed machine at home | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: learned a skill | sphere: arts.U | chance: 71
- B | book the bands into a bigger room, and take a share of the door | v: achievement, power | sphere: arts.B | chance: 69
- R | queue round the block every Friday and dance until the lights come on | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: arts.R | chance: 75
- G | keep to the old tunes night at the local, and let the young have their noise | v: tradition, security | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: arts.G | chance: 74
- BR | put on a night of your own in an empty warehouse, and fill it | v: achievement, hedonism | lever: found | pushes: place | sphere: arts.BR | chance: 42
- UG | mix a song your grandmother sang into the new sound | v: tradition, self-direction | sphere: arts.GU | chance: 50
- UR | form a band with friends, and play the new sound your own way | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: found | pushes: group scene | sphere: arts.UR | chance: 48
- WB | lend the band your van and your savings for their first record | v: benevolence, achievement | lever: fund | pushes: group scene | sphere: arts.WB | chance: 60
- WG | ask the neighbours who complain about the noise to come along one night | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: arts.GW | chance: 42
works: The sound becomes {Ns} sound, and the friends from that queue are friends for life.
works: Years later, a few bars of it on the radio and {N} is back on that dance floor.
fails: The clubs are shut by spring after complaints, and the scene moves on without {N}.
fails: {N} is out every night for a year, and the work and the sleep pay for it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- scene_sells (pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event scene_sells, selector members, share .5
== the first club is a chain bar now
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: scene_sells
share: .5
haunt: arts.song
ladder: regular
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: scene_sells (sphere arts). Selector members: a scene outgrows its first rooms and the media and the labels take it up; about half of its old crowd feel it as a turn in their own life, a deal, a loss or both (share .5, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: years in a scene, a scene that has grown famous, a friend in one of its bands
rarer: a person who never belonged to a scene, a small town far from the labels
tone: mixed
life: friends, interests, money
horizon: years
roles: friend, colleague
earth: the sound of your youth is in every advert now, the first club is a chain bar, and the old crowd have moved on
scene: The sound {N} danced to at twenty is in every advert now. The first club is a chain bar, {friend} has signed with a big label, and an agency has rung to ask {N} to help sell the old days.
scene W: The scene had one rule: everyone in, nobody above the crowd. {N} watches the old friends sort themselves into the signed and the rest.
scene U: {N} can hear exactly what the label changed: the rough edges sanded off, the strange bit cut. It works, and that is the sad part.
scene B: The money has arrived, and it will not stay long. {N} knows which old names the agencies will pay for.
scene R: The adverts, the chain bar, the shiny new versions. {N} feels as if someone has stolen a summer and sold it back.
scene G: {N} still has the first flyers in a box and the old songs in the head. They belong to the people who were there.
- W | turn the agency down, and ask the old crowd not to sell the old days either | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: arts.W | chance: 70
- U | write down how the scene really began, before the adverts rewrite it | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: arts.U | chance: 73
- B | take the agency's fee and help them sell the old days, on your terms | v: achievement, power | sphere: arts.B | chance: 75
- R | throw a party with the rough old records, the way they used to sound | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: arts.R | chance: 74
- G | keep the first flyers and the old songs for the people who were there | v: tradition, security | lever: loyalty | sphere: arts.G | chance: 69
- RG | find the cellar where the next sound is starting, and dance there instead | v: stimulation, hedonism | lever: exit | pushes: group scene | sphere: arts.RG | chance: 54
- UB | study what the label changed, and sell your own old tracks the same way | v: achievement, power | sphere: arts.UB | chance: 56
- UR | remix the old songs rougher than ever, and post them for free | v: self-direction, stimulation | tech: internet | sphere: arts.UR | chance: 56
- WB | ask your signed friend to put the unsigned bands on the bill | v: benevolence, power | sphere: arts.WB | chance: 52
- WG | gather the old crowd for a reunion night, signed and unsigned alike | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: arts.GW | chance: 66
works: {N} comes out of it with a fair share, of money or of memory, and the friends that mattered.
works: Years later the old crowd meet again, and the songs sound like theirs once more.
fails: The friends who signed and the friends who did not stop speaking, and {N} is caught between.
fails: {N} hears the sound of {Ns} youth selling soap, and cannot hear it any other way again.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- work_banned (pairs D4b)

# world: sphere event work_banned, selector place, share .4
== the film they pulled from the cinemas
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: work_banned
share: .4
haunt: arts.screen
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-40
times: World event: work_banned (sphere arts). Selector place: a censor or a campaign pulls a work in a time of low speech rights, war, a strict faith law or a satire that hit home; about 4 in 10 of the people living there feel the loss of a work they love, or a choice about seeing it (share .4, estimate), a few times in a life (estimate)
likelier: weak speech rights, a strict faith law, a person who loves films
rarer: a free country in calm years, a person who never goes to the cinema
tone: trouble
life: friends, community, law
horizon: months
roles: friend, parent
earth: a film you love is pulled from the cinemas after a campaign against it, and copies spread from phone to phone
scene: A film {N} loves has been pulled from the cinemas after a campaign against it. Within days copies are spreading from phone to phone, and {friend} has one, and a room to watch it in.
scene W: The law now says the film may not be shown. {N} thinks a law is a law, and also that this one may be wrong.
scene U: {N} has read what the campaign says the film shows. Most of it is not in the film at all.
scene B: Banned things sell. {N} knows that a copy of the film is worth more this week than last.
scene R: Nobody tells {N} what to watch. The ban only makes {N} want to see it more.
scene G: {parent} says some things are better not shown, and the old family friends agree. {N} is not so sure.
- W | keep the ban, and write to the board to ask why it was made | v: conformity, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: arts.W | chance: 66
- U | set the campaign's claims beside what the film really shows | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: arts.U | chance: 67
- B | sell copies of the film from your phone, at a price | v: achievement, power | mark: broke the law | lever: subvert | sphere: arts.B | chance: 79
- R | watch it with your friend in the back room, and talk about it all night | v: stimulation, hedonism | mark: defied an authority | lever: subvert | sphere: arts.R | chance: 76
- G | let the film go, and keep the peace with your family | v: tradition, conformity | sphere: arts.G | chance: 66
- BR | project the film on a wall in the square one night, and slip away | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: defied an authority | lever: subvert | pushes: state | sphere: arts.BR | chance: 38
- UB | find out who paid for the campaign, and what they wanted from it | v: power, security | sphere: arts.UB | chance: 56
- UG | keep a copy hidden safely, for the day the ban is lifted | v: tradition, security | mark: broke the law | sphere: arts.GU | chance: 62
- WG | talk the film through with your family at the kitchen table, in your own words | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: arts.GW | chance: 58
- WR | sign the open letter against the ban, with your name in full | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: arts.RW | chance: 62
works: The ban is lifted within a year, and {N} sees the film again on a big screen with a full house.
works: {N} keeps faith with the film and with the people who matter, and comes through without trouble.
fails: The police knock on a door in {Ns} street over a copy of the film, and everyone grows careful.
fails: The arguments over the film split {Ns} family, and nobody mentions it at dinner for a year.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- last_teller (pairs D1a)

# world: sphere event last_teller, selector members, share .5
== the last voice that knew the old songs
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: last_teller
share: .5
haunt: arts.tale
who: elder
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 20-50
times: World event: last_teller (sphere arts). Selector members: the elder who knew a family's or a people's old tellings dies with few pupils; about half of the kin and neighbours who heard them face the question of what to keep (share .5, estimate), once in a life for most who meet it (estimate)
likelier: a family or a people with its own songs or tongue, a thin tradition, an elder who sang
rarer: a family whose old songs died out long ago, a person far from kin
tone: trouble
life: family, loss, community
horizon: years
roles: elder, parent
earth: your great-aunt, the last who sang the old songs in the old tongue, has died, and the recordings were on a lost phone
scene: {Ns} great-aunt, the last in the family who sang the old songs in the old tongue, has died. Someone once recorded her singing, but the recordings were on a phone that was lost years ago.
scene W: At the funeral the family stands in silence where the old mourning song should be. Nobody knows the words.
scene U: {N} remembers fragments: a tune, a refrain, two lines of a verse. With care, some of it could be pieced together.
scene B: A university once offered to pay her to record the songs. {N} wonders if they kept anything.
scene R: {N} keeps hearing her voice at the kitchen table, loud and off-key and wonderful. The silence is hard to bear.
scene G: Those songs came down through ten generations, and they stopped with her. {N} feels the weight of that.
- W | gather the family to sing together at the funeral, whatever anyone remembers | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: arts.W | chance: 65
- U | piece the songs together from fragments, old letters and notebooks | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: arts.U | chance: 62
- B | ask the university for any recording they made, and offer to pay for a copy | v: achievement, security | sphere: arts.B | chance: 52
- R | sing the one verse you know at the wake, loud and off-key, the way she did | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: arts.R | chance: 65
- G | ask the oldest neighbours who heard her to teach you what they can | v: tradition | mark: learned a skill | lever: loyalty | sphere: arts.G | chance: 48
- BG | let the songs go, and keep her in the stories the family still tells | v: security, tradition | lever: neglect | sphere: arts.BG | chance: 80
- BR | make a song of your own about her, and play it wherever they will have you | v: self-direction, achievement | sphere: arts.BR | chance: 52
- UG | write down every line anyone remembers, with the tunes, for the children | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: arts.GU | chance: 60
- WR | start a yearly night in her name where anyone may sing what they remember | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: found | sphere: arts.RW | chance: 54
- WU | take up the old tongue properly, with lessons, so the songs can be sung again | v: tradition, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | sphere: arts.WU | chance: 52
works: Enough of the songs come back, pieced together, that the children learn three of them by heart.
works: {N} grieves her properly, and carries one song of hers for the rest of {Ns} life.
fails: Nothing more is found, and the songs are gone beyond recall.
fails: The family argues over what she really sang, and the quarrel outlives the grief.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- old_songs_return (pairs D2b)

# world: sphere event old_songs_return, selector place, share .3
== the folk festival in the field
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: old_songs_return
share: .3
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 5-20
times: World event: old_songs_return (sphere arts). Selector place: a people feeling uprooted or newly proud takes up its thin old songs again, and a folk festival fills a field; about 3 in 10 of the people living there go and are drawn in (share .3, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: a family with its own songs, a grandparent who still sings, a time of pride or uprooting
rarer: a family with no old songs, a person who dislikes crowds
tone: joy
life: family, community, interests
horizon: week
roles: grandparent, friend
earth: a folk festival fills a field for a weekend, and teenagers learn the old dances from grandparents in the queue
scene: A folk festival fills a field outside {place} for a weekend. Teenagers learn the old dances from grandparents in the queue for food, and the small stage asks anyone who knows an old song to come up.
scene W: The last night ends with one song the whole field sings together. {N} wants to know the words by then.
scene U: Half the tunes have five versions, and the old players argue over which is true. {N} wants to hear them all.
scene B: The craft stalls sell out by noon. {N} sees that the old songs have become something people pay for.
scene R: The fiddles start up and the plank floor shakes. {N} cannot keep still.
scene G: {grandparent} used to sing one of these songs at the kitchen table. Hearing it here, with a thousand people, {N} has to sit down.
- W | learn the closing song's words, and sing it with the whole field on the last night | v: tradition, conformity | sphere: arts.W | chance: 80
- U | go round the old players with a notebook, and write down every version of a tune | v: universalism, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | sphere: arts.U | chance: 67
- B | sell the family's old craft at a stall, and come home with an order book | v: achievement | sphere: arts.B | chance: 76
- R | dance every set until the band packs up | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: arts.R | chance: 69
- G | go up on the small stage and sing the song you learned at home | v: tradition, achievement | sphere: arts.G | chance: 61
- RG | learn the old dance from a grandmother in the food queue, and teach your friends | v: tradition, hedonism | mark: made a friend | sphere: arts.RG | chance: 78
- UB | ask the organisers how the festival pays, and what it would take to run one | v: achievement, self-direction | sphere: arts.UB | chance: 66
- UG | record the oldest singers on your phone, with their names and their stories | v: tradition, universalism | tech: phone | sphere: arts.GU | chance: 74
- WB | pay for a coach so the care home's old folk can come for a day | v: benevolence | lever: fund | sphere: arts.WB | chance: 56
- WR | join the procession with the town's banner and the drums | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: arts.RW | chance: 58
works: {N} comes home with a song, a dance and a reason to go back next year.
works: The old songs are sung at the next family gathering, and the young ones know the words.
fails: It rains for three days, and {N} goes home soaked and sore with little to show for it.
fails: The old players quarrel about who sings it right, and the young ones drift back to their phones.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- work_of_the_day (pairs D4a)

# world: sphere event work_of_the_day, selector all, share .4
== the series with the ending nobody agrees on
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: work_of_the_day
share: .4
haunt: arts.screen
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 13-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 3-10
times: World event: work_of_the_day (sphere arts). Selector all: a series or a show reaches nearly everyone while its question is ripe in the culture; about 4 in 10 people argue about it with someone close and feel a view of theirs shift or harden (share .4, estimate), a few times in a life (estimate)
likelier: a series everyone watches, a question splitting the country, a family that argues at dinner
rarer: a person who watches nothing, a remote place
tone: mixed
life: friends, family, work
horizon: months
roles: friend, parent
earth: everyone is watching the same series, and at work, at dinner and online the argument about its ending will not stop
scene: Everyone is watching the same series. At work, at dinner and online the argument about its ending will not stop, and {friend} wants to know which side {N} is on.
scene W: The ending asks what people owe each other. {N} keeps thinking about it on the way home.
scene U: {N} has watched the last episode twice. The clues were there all along, if anyone had looked.
scene B: Everyone has an opinion and nobody is listening. {N} notices whose opinion gets repeated.
scene R: {N} shouted at the screen in the last ten minutes, and is still angry about it.
scene G: {parent} says it was rubbish and the old shows were better. {N} is not sure the old shows asked anything at all.
- W | say what you think at dinner, and listen to every side of the table | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: arts.W | chance: 75
- U | write a long post showing how the clues pointed to the ending all along | v: self-direction, achievement | tech: internet | sphere: arts.U | chance: 74
- B | keep your view to yourself, and agree with whoever matters in the room | v: security, conformity | sphere: arts.B | chance: 75
- R | argue it out with your friend until one of you storms off | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: arts.R | chance: 74
- G | turn it off and watch the old shows with your family instead | v: tradition, security | sphere: arts.G | chance: 66
- BG | say plainly it was only a story, and change the subject to the weekend | v: security, hedonism | sphere: arts.BG | chance: 66
- RG | hold a watch party for the last episode, with food and the whole street | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: arts.RG | chance: 66
- UR | make a short video of your own ending, and see who shares it | v: self-direction, stimulation | tech: internet | sphere: arts.UR | chance: 50
- WB | get a speaker to the community centre to talk about the question it asks | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: arts.WB | chance: 48
- WU | start a reading group on the book the series came from | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: found | sphere: arts.WU | chance: 66
works: The argument changes {Ns} mind about something, and {N} is glad it did.
works: {N} and {friend} end up laughing about it, and watch the next series together.
fails: A joke about the ending goes down badly, and it is a chilly month at home.
fails: {N} digs in, and an old view hardens into something harder to shift.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- patron_builds (pairs D6a)

# world: sphere event patron_builds, selector place, share .25
== the arts centre in the old station
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: patron_builds
share: .25
haunt: arts.stage
who: patron
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 15-40
times: World event: patron_builds (sphere arts). Selector place: a new fortune pays for a stage or an arts centre in a boom, with a thin public purse; about 1 in 4 of the people living there find a job, a seat or an audition in it (share .25, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: a boom town, a rich family seeking standing, a person who sings, acts or builds sets
rarer: a poor town with no rich families, a person who never goes out
tone: joy
life: work, interests, community
horizon: years
roles: friend, patron
earth: a new fortune pays for an arts centre in the old station, and the founder's name is on everything
scene: A new fortune has paid for an arts centre in the old station. The founder's name is on the doors, the seats and the cups, and the centre is hiring backstage, selling cheap seats and holding open auditions.
scene W: The centre wants a town choir for its opening night. {N} likes the thought of the whole town singing in one hall.
scene U: The centre has a proper rehearsal room and a piano that is in tune. {N} would give a lot for an hour in it each week.
scene B: The founder means to be remembered, and needs people who can make that happen. {N} sees a job with a future.
scene R: Open auditions on Saturday, for anyone at all. {N} has been waiting for a stage like this.
scene G: The old station was where {Ns} family waved off the trains. {N} wonders if the new place will remember that.
- W | join the town choir for the opening night, and learn your part by heart | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: arts.W | chance: 69
- U | ask for an hour a week in the rehearsal room, and use every minute | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | sphere: arts.U | chance: 71
- B | apply for the job running the founder's programme | v: achievement, power | sphere: arts.B | chance: 58
- R | go to the open auditions on Saturday and give it everything | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: arts.R | chance: 67
- G | ask the centre to hang the old station photos in the foyer | v: tradition | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: arts.G | chance: 55
- BG | take a job backstage shifting sets, and keep your eyes open | v: security, achievement | sphere: arts.BG | chance: 78
- UG | offer to make a show of the old station's history from the families' stories | v: tradition, self-direction | sphere: arts.GU | chance: 48
- UR | pitch the centre a strange new show nobody has seen before | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: arts.UR | chance: 46
- WB | sit on the centre's board, and see that the cheap seats stay cheap | v: power, universalism | lever: lead | pushes: place | sphere: arts.WB | chance: 42
- WR | start a youth theatre in the centre that anyone can join for free | v: universalism, stimulation | lever: found | pushes: place | sphere: arts.RW | chance: 56
works: The centre becomes part of {Ns} week, and some of {Ns} best nights are there.
works: A door opens at the centre, and {N} walks through it into work or a part.
fails: The founder loses interest after three years, and the centre fills with weddings and conferences.
fails: {N} is turned down, and watches the opening night from the cheap seats with a sour heart.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- stages_go_dark (pairs D5a)

# world: sphere event stages_go_dark, selector members, share .5
== the venues close and the band plays kitchens
tier: life event
sphere: arts
sphere_event: stages_go_dark
share: .5
haunt: arts.song
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-75
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 8-25
times: World event: stages_go_dark (sphere arts). Selector members: a slump closes the theatres and venues as wages and patrons' money fall; about half of the players and backstage hands who worked there feel their own work dry up (share .5, estimate), once or twice in a working life (estimate)
likelier: a slump, a person who plays, acts or works backstage for money, a town with few venues
rarer: a person with a steady day job, a boom year
tone: trouble
life: work, money, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, colleague
earth: the slump closes two theatres and the music venue, and your band plays kitchen parties instead
scene: The slump has closed two theatres and the music venue in {place}. The bookings have dried up, and {Ns} band is down to kitchen parties, for a plate of food and whatever goes in the hat.
scene W: The council is paying a few idle players to give free concerts in the square. {N} could put in for it.
scene U: Practice still matters, slump or not. {N} has more hours than ever, and nowhere to play.
scene B: {N} has rent to pay. A song is worth what someone will pay for it, and this month nobody can.
scene R: Kitchens, cellars, back gardens: {N} will play anywhere there is a crowd. The best nights of the year pay nothing at all.
